{"table":"evidence","ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/evidence/fixed_time_spatial_warrant_20261025","record":{"id":"fixed_time_spatial_warrant_20261025","kind":"semantic_review","status":"not_run","command":[],"tool":"Authored source comparison; independent semantic acceptance not run","source_ids":["authored_long_comparisons_20261024","support_source_sample_jets","support_source_coercive_moments","support_tex_regularity","scalar-r2-26-source-order-parameter-regularity"],"subject_ids":["support.fixed_time_spatial_coercivity","support.integrated_coercivity","support.regularity","support.diffusion","support.positive_curvature","scalar.constant_curvature","scalar.smooth_positive_density"],"details":"The long-record reconstruction extracts the spatial inequality used in order-parameter-regularity.tex:116–150: replace the coefficient by c at one shrinking neighborhood, preserve monotonicity, choose a fixed compact strip and common L1 bound, and pass derivatives through order four evaluated along coupled paths. Minimality supplies none of this transfer; it is used in the density consumer to establish smoothness, c>0 and moment saturation. On a positive plateau the third-time-derivative identity supplies the curvature consumer. Separately, SampleJets.lean:135–143 gives the scaled inequality for the SKSupport canonical diffusion at a positive continuity time; lines 90–133 supply its two dominated-convergence limits and CoerciveMoments.lean:15–17 fixes the powers of c. Division by c^2 for c>0 produces the normalized common expression. These are source-located mathematical warrants, not extracted dependency edges, a checked cross-model transport, or formal acceptance."},"usage":{"record_ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/evidence/fixed_time_spatial_warrant_20261025","paper_focus":[],"paper_memberships":[{"stage":"long","subgraph_ref":"sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f